    "answer": {
      "short": "$120$",
      "worked": "Different subsets of these distinct primes give different products, by unique prime factorisation. Exclude the empty subset and the seven one-element subsets.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=2^7-\\binom{7}{0}-\\binom{7}{1}\\\\N&=128-1-7=120.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
